-- title:
--   Gauss prime of the pole chart is a minimal prime
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma\le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ be of finite index and let $p$ be a prime. Assume the $q$-expansion `jqModC ℚ` of the modular invariant, namely $q^{-1}$ times the power series $E_4^3\eta^{-24}$ with rational coefficients, lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the subfield of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the ratios $\hat f/\hat g$ of $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ having integral coefficients; write $F=$ `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ Γ` for the corresponding field for $\Gamma$, $j\in F$ for the element with that $q$-expansion, and $\mathcal O=$ `chartAlgInf p Γ hj` for the subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over the `R p`-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$. Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ which is an `R p`-algebra, and let $\mathrm{red}\colon\mathcal O\to \kappa((q))$ be a ring homomorphism which is coefficientwise reduction, in the sense that whenever $y\in (\mathrm{R}\,p)((q))$ has image in $\mathbb Q((q))$ equal to the Laurent series underlying $b\in\mathcal O$, then $\mathrm{red}(b)$ is the image of $y$ under coefficientwise application of $\mathrm{R}\,p\to\kappa$. Let $\mathrm{ev}\colon \kappa\otimes_{\mathrm{R}\,p}\mathcal O\to\kappa$ be a $\kappa$-algebra map with $\mathrm{ev}(1\otimes b)$ the constant coefficient of $\mathrm{red}(b)$. Then the ideal of $\kappa\otimes_{\mathrm{R}\,p}\mathcal O$ generated by the image of $\ker(\mathrm{red})$ under $b\mapsto 1\otimes b$ is a minimal prime of $\kappa\otimes_{\mathrm{R}\,p}\mathcal O$, and it is contained in $\ker(\mathrm{ev})$.
--
--   The kernel of $\mathrm{red}$ is the centre on the pole chart $\mathcal O$ of the Gauss valuation of $F$ at $p$, and the assertion is that its extension to the geometric fibre $\kappa\otimes\mathcal O$ is one of the minimal primes of that fibre — the generic point of a component through the reduced cusp, at which the evaluation map $\mathrm{ev}$ is supported. It is used in [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.mem_range_comp_zero_iff_map_ker_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.mem_range_comp_zero_iff_map_ker_le) in the study of the fibre at $p$ of the two-chart integral model of the modular curve near the cusp.
